format 1

# Workflows for nix-orca (`release` node). actlith v0.1.0 kinds cannot meet
# this repository's rules, so every workflow is hand-written and listed
# here with its reason; `actlith check` holds the directory to this list.

## workflows
id|kind|systems|cache|args

## hand-written
path|reason
.github/workflows/gate.yml|the `gate` kind pushes all a job builds or reads no cache; darwin and dev-shell paths are never pushed (root V5), so this one reads the cache only
.github/workflows/build.yml|the `build` kind pushes every system and refuses x86_64-darwin; only Linux orca-ide closures are pushed (root V5), and x86_64-darwin builds under Rosetta (D39)
.github/workflows/upstream.yml|the bump PR comes from a GitHub App token so it triggers the build (round 8), and a moved upstream tag opens an issue (round 9); the `upstream` kind does neither
.github/workflows/release.yml|no release kind in actlith v0.1.0; text-only release with attested NAR hashes, idempotent per tag (round 8)
.github/workflows/agents.yml|the agent-input PR comes from a GitHub App token so it triggers the build (round 8) and never merges itself (round 9); `update-pins` does neither
